// Three exponential means in a row, combined so that the lag of a straight line
// cancels exactly rather than merely shrinking.
//
// Exercises: three averages each taken over the previous one's output, which is
// where the warmup comes from, and an association written the way the study
// states it. Three of one mean less three of the second plus the third is the
// same quantity in exact arithmetic and a different number in binary64, so the
// brackets here are part of the study rather than a matter of taste, and the
// library's own triple mean uses the other arrangement.

version 1

study("Triple exponential average", overlay = true, precision = 4)

len = input(9, "Length", min = 1, max = 1000)

once   = ema(close, len)
twice  = ema(once, len)
thrice = ema(twice, len)

plot(3 * (once - twice) + thrice, "Triple", aqua, width = 2)
